# Tight Lines clients (website vs iOS)

This repo has **no** iOS or website UI. Tight Lines consumes this API from two angler clients:

- Website (Jinja / HTML)
- Expo iOS app (`tight_lines_app/mobile/`)

## Do this

- Keep `/api/locations`, `/api/tides/{id}`, `/api/weather/{id}`, and any new angler endpoints usable by **both** Tight Lines clients with the same JSON contract.
- When extending the API for a Tight Lines feature, assume website and iOS should both be able to call it (feature parity lives in Tight Lines, not here).

## Do not

- Add admin-only or operator consoles to this service for a mobile app.
- Invent a second payload shape “for iOS” when the website already consumes the same resource.
- Put user-management, catalogue CRUD, or moderation in this weather app — that belongs on the **Tight Lines website**, not iOS and not here.

Native-only iOS behaviour (push, camera, offline) does not require weather-API changes unless the shared contract truly needs a new field.
